Relevant columns, their potential usage, and the conditions that will be applied  

• objects.object_id: join key between objects and images  
• objects.department: filter for the value ‘Photographs’  
• objects.object_name: keep rows whose name contains the word ‘Photograph’  
• objects.artist_display_name: eliminate “unknown” artists (e.g. NOT ILIKE ‘unknown%’)  
• objects.object_end_date: require a date ≤ 1839  
• objects.title: one of the required result columns  
• objects.medium: one of the required result columns  
• images.object_id: join key coming from images  
• images.original_image_url: the required URL column  

Conditions to be used  

1. objects.department = 'Photographs'  
2. LOWER(objects.object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'  
3. LOWER(objects.artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%'  
4. objects.object_end_date <= 1839  

─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  
Ten exploratory → final SQL queries  
(Every query ends with LIMIT 20)  

```sql
-- 1) Peek at the Photographs department
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE department = 'Photographs'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Find object names that actually contain the word “Photograph”
SELECT object_id, object_name, department
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE department = 'Photographs'
  AND LOWER(object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Inspect artist names, making sure “unknown” can be filtered out
SELECT DISTINCT artist_display_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE department = 'Photographs'
  AND LOWER(object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Check the oldest photographs (≤ 1839)
SELECT object_id, object_name, artist_display_name, object_end_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE department = 'Photographs'
  AND LOWER(object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
  AND object_end_date <= 1839
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Join one candidate object to its image to see the URL shape
SELECT o.object_id,
       i.original_image_url
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects` AS o
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.images`  AS i
  ON o.object_id = i.object_id
WHERE o.department = 'Photographs'
  AND LOWER(o.object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Count how many qualifying objects have at least one image URL
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT o.object_id) AS photograph_objects_with_images
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects` AS o
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.images`  AS i
  ON o.object_id = i.object_id
WHERE o.department = 'Photographs'
  AND LOWER(o.object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
  AND o.object_end_date <= 1839
  AND LOWER(o.artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%';
```

```sql
-- 7) Pull titles & mediums along with one URL per object (simple JOIN)
SELECT DISTINCT o.object_id,
       o.title,
       o.artist_display_name,
       o.medium,
       i.original_image_url
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects` AS o
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.images`  AS i
  ON o.object_id = i.object_id
WHERE o.department = 'Photographs'
  AND LOWER(o.object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
  AND o.object_end_date <= 1839
  AND LOWER(o.artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Same as #7 but ordering oldest first
SELECT DISTINCT o.object_id,
       o.title,
       o.artist_display_name,
       o.medium,
       i.original_image_url
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects` AS o
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.images`  AS i
  ON o.object_id = i.object_id
WHERE o.department = 'Photographs'
  AND LOWER(o.object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
  AND o.object_end_date <= 1839
  AND LOWER(o.artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%'
ORDER BY o.object_end_date
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) For each object pick only one (the first) URL using ARRAY_AGG
WITH candidates AS (
  SELECT o.object_id,
         o.title,
         o.artist_display_name,
         o.medium,
         ARRAY_AGG(i.original_image_url ORDER BY i.original_image_url)[OFFSET(0)] AS one_url
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects` AS o
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.images`  AS i
    ON o.object_id = i.object_id
  WHERE o.department = 'Photographs'
    AND LOWER(o.object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
    AND o.object_end_date <= 1839
    AND LOWER(o.artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%'
  GROUP BY o.object_id, o.title, o.artist_display_name, o.medium
)
SELECT *
FROM candidates
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL ANSWER: titles, artist names, mediums, and original image URLs
SELECT o.title,
       o.artist_display_name AS artist_name,
       o.medium,
       i.original_image_url
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects` AS o
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.images`  AS i
  ON o.object_id = i.object_id
WHERE o.department = 'Photographs'
  AND LOWER(o.object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
  AND o.object_end_date <= 1839
  AND LOWER(o.artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%'
LIMIT 20;
```
